There has been much discussion recently on possible additions
for the next version.  I like to add some comments about
spellbooks.  Currently there seems to be a bias against the use
of spells.  The books are heavy, they're limited in use
(although better than single use scrolls), and they use up food.

The problem is that once you have the AoY, they're pretty much
ineffective, so their utility is early in the game.
Unfortunately, the requirements of being high enough
experience, intelligence, and luck means that they're not
possible for early characters.  This in my mind limits their
utility to the middle part of the game.  Thus, a player cannot
develop magic skill for later use because it won't work.

My suggestions would be to reduce the number.  Get rid of some
of the ones that are repeats of other functions.  This will
allow someone to have a better chance of accumulating the
really useful ones.  My favorites have been

	identify
	remove curse
	magic mapping
	fireball (great for the kraken and when surrounded by
monsters)
	knock
	magic missile

Allow them to be used indefinitely.  To preserve balance make
each succeeding time the spellbook is read require more power
for casting the spell.

Allow spellcasting after the AoY is obtained.  Perhaps some
other article (like some sort of confused enchanted GDSM or CoMP
be required to make the spell work.

After the AoY is obtained, the game becomes one of combat to
get past everything in your way.

Comments?

Mike K


